TITLE='Authentic title "This Setup Only Happens Once Every 50 Years — It\'s Happening Again" is a rare-event, pattern-recurrence promise. The script compares 1971-1982 with 2026 across three "traps" (safe money, crowded trade, entry price) and ends on valuation rather than a crash call. TYPICAL against the cohort (1.125x; 5-peer 1.496x, also TYPICAL, so the tier is stable). Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background. Left: a smiling cartoon man in a white polo holding cash. Right: a heavy black headline "BUY NOW!" over a line chart with red-labelled peaks "1929", "1973" and "2026" with a "WE ARE HERE" dot followed by a steep red drop. At 320x180 the headline and dates stay legible. The "BUY NOW!" plus crash arrow conflicts with the script\'s argument (keep buying through flat markets; current prices are expensive) and with its explicit "not financial advice"; 1929 never appears in the script.'
SCRIPT='A historical-comparison essay: gas-price hook; Nixon shock and price controls; OPEC embargo; the Rileys (composite family); trap one: safe money (1970s inflation, T-bills, Regulation Q, 1973-74 crash, flat Dow 1966-82, mortgage rate shock 7.5% vs 18.63%); trap two: crowded trade (gold 1971-80-99, energy weight); 2026 parallels (Iran/Hormuz, debt, interest, Fed, real wages, gold and silver drawdowns); trap three: entry price (1982 CAPE 6.5 vs ~41, yields 6.24% vs 1.05%, concentration, Polaroid); counter-arguments (anchored 5y5y expectations, low unionisation, US oil production); age-dependent implications; Rileys\' DCA and $804,000; close. FRED-verified: 1970s inflation peaks and cumulative figures, 18.63% mortgage record, both mortgage payments, 5y5y 2.32%, debt level. Overstated: debt growth "$91,549 per second". 2026 geopolitical and precious-metal figures unverified. The stored ending is complete.'
